WEBVTT

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.790
Asuka, there's big trouble!

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:24.750
Another Disas is attacking the town, chu!

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.230
Those damned Disas...

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.380
How could they do that
to our peaceful city?

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.440
I'll stop them!

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.090
Transform with your Magical Karambit, chu!

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:53.890
Magical Girl Rapture Asuka,

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:55.620
here to save the day!

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.780
<i>January 2016.</i>

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:04.180
<i>A world of lifeforms hostile to humanity,</i>

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:05.570
<i>the Disas,</i>

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:08.210
<i>began a stealth invasion
of the human world.</i>

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:13.580
<i>In February 2017,
another world that opposed the Disas,</i>

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.110
<i>the Spirit Realm,</i>

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.470
<i>formed a military alliance with Earth,</i>

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:25.230
<i>and created the Spirit Realm Treaty
Organization to aid humanity.</i>

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:28.480
<i>This resulted in the creation
of the so-called "Magical Girls,"</i>

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:34.440
<i>girls who could synchronize with
spirits to gain special powers.</i>

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:37.600
<i>Despite their beauty,</i>

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:42.130
<i>the battlefield these young girls found
themselves on was a brutal one.</i>

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:01.680
Mt. Aso, Kumamoto Prefecture, Kyushu

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:19.710
An ally?

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.780
Iizuka, with the JGSDF.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:25.650
Constantince Asimov. I'm with the GRU.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.060
Iizuka of the JGSDF...

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.130
You were part of the 
Special Operations Group?

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:32.800
That arm...

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:33.980
You okay?

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.030
Yeah.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.380
The drugs have kicked in.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.390
I don't feel a lot of pain,

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.760
but my head feels like it's full of fuzz.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:42.980
I see.

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:46.120
I don't think there are any enemies left.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.990
Operation Code Whiskey Charlie

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:51.770
has reached the final rendezvous point.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.820
How many are left?

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:55.700
That I don't know.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:00.210
It's pathetic.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:03.210
All the best soldiers from
around the world together,

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:07.670
and in the end, all we can
do is rely on nine little girls.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.800
We can't even provide fire support.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.100
There's nothing we can do about it.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:13.210
This fight is beyond normal
human understanding.

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:17.620
Those kids are the only ones
who can save the world.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:25.710
So that's the Disas Beast?
The king of the Disas...

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:26.640
Oh no...

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.430
It's huge!

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.800
There were nine of us when
we started. Only we five are left.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.590
Claudia...

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.010
Magdalena...

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.340
Crystal...

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:38.500
Patricia...

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.320
We have to fight our hardest

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.410
for the sake of those who died, too.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.910
It's finally time, ladies.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.310
No matter how big it is, it's still a Disas.

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:53.500
It has to have a crystal vein somewhere.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:57.370
Get me close to it.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:00.210
Then I'll rip it apart.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:03.900
I don't like letting
you take over the finale,

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:07.180
but I can't see us winning
this any other way.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:11.400
Kurumi, put all of your remaining healing
resources into the magical syringe.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.350
Right...

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:20.900
Now let's say our motto...

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:24.490
Who laughs last laughs best.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.200
Let's go!

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:29.140
Face-off!

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:45.130
<b>The Magical Girl Comes Back</b>

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:52.600
Three
Years
Later

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.980
Dizzy?

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:00.070
Something like that.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.310
You probably need
more iron in your diet.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.640
Suck on a ten yen piece!

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:07.130
But that's not iron! That's bronze!

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.530
It's not good for you!

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:12.450
Anyway, shouldn't you be
out there, Nozo-chan?

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.530
Our class is gonna lose.

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:17.500
Nah, they're fine.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.480
That transfer student's amazing.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:24.940
Otori Asuka-san, right?

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:29.430
Her swimming and marathon times 
ranked in the inter-high championships.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:31.510
Are you curious about our transfer student?

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.570
No, I don't know...

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:35.940
Um...

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:38.900
An aloof transfer student,

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.220
incredibly athletic, who transfers
in at an odd time in freshman year.

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:45.980
Think she's the heroine
of a late-night anime?

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:47.720
A late-night anime?

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:52.300
Sure, she's mysterious, but...

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:55.410
I wonder what she does
when she's not at school?

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:15.330
<i>What appeared to be a
Magical Girl was sighted</i>

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:18.480
<b>A Magical Girl at the Scene 
of a Drug Cartel's Demise?</b>

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:18.480
<i>during anti-cartel
operations in Mexico City.</i>

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.910
<i>According to experts,</i>

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:24.290
<i>the person in this photo
is likely Mia Cyrus,</i>

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:27.790
<i>a member of the American military.</i>

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:30.130
<i>Mia Cyrus is one of the Magical Five,</i>

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:33.740
<i>who brought an end to the 
Distonian War three years ago...</i>

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.730
Mommy, look! A Magical Girl!

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:35.550
It's a Magical Girl, Mommy!

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:36.830
Right, right.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.810
Come on, you want a balloon, right?

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:40.410
Mr. Kitty is waiting.

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:05.550
Mommy, I want to be a Magical Girl, too!

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.650
You don't want to be a Magical Girl.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:09.020
It's dangerous!

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:13.620
I wish I could get her to join our team.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.770
Who? The transfer student?

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:16.900
That's right.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:18.580
Her body, the way she moves...

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.560
She's used it a lot.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.880
You mean she's trained a lot, right?

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:26.020
Hey, you.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.220
There's no smoking on this street.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.830
You hit her foot with your cigarette butt.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.180
I didn't mean to.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.540
Of course not.

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.550
You almost burned her!

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.050
Nozo-chan, that's enough.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:41.640
Apologize to my friend.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:43.710
Shut up.

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:47.530
You're a grown-up, right?

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:48.660
Let me go.

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:52.700
It's your fault for grabbing me.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:00.910
<i>Do I snap his arm
and then strangle him?</i>

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:03.370
<i>Bring my elbow down
on the back of his head...</i>

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.720
If you're a grown-up, then act like it.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:16.930
It's embarrassing.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:20.790
Umm...

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:37.980
Hey, Otori Asuka-san...

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.240
Thanks so much for
your help this morning.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.870
Asuka-san, you're
super-athletic, aren't you?

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:48.210
Oh, I'm Makino Nozomi.

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.190
And four-eyes here is Hata Sayoko.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:53.170
Hey, don't introduce me as "four-eyes."

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:54.830
But you wear glasses, right?

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:56.840
Sure, but...

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:59.490
Can I push my desk up against yours?

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:01.350
Let's eat lunch together.

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:04.210
O-Okay, I guess.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:12.860
It's so good.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:14.820
Hey...

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:16.820
Asuka-san,

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.070
are you a former assassin or something?

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.220
What are you talking about?

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:25.990
The way you knocked that
guy over this morning...

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:28.020
You seemed like a real pro!

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:30.370
I used to do aikido.

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:33.130
Um...

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:35.740
I've been wondering.

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:39.470
Otori-san, you spend a lot of
time reading books by yourself.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:40.670
And?

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:45.100
<b>Franz on the Waves</b>

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:42.760
I love books, too.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:45.100
That's a great book, isn't it?

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:47.820
Do you like books?

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:51.110
You don't, Otori-san?

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:54.240
I don't know.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.240
I don't think it's that I like them.

00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:01.370
It just keeps me from remembering bad things.

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:08.200
Sorry.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:10.040
I know that's a weird thing to say.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.540
I guess I don't talk to a lot of people.

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:17.450
Well, enough book talk.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:19.010
Join the track team!

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:20.970
The track team?

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:22.040
Yup!

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:24.980
Your body, your legs... your breasts!

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:27.320
You need to put them all to good use!

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:29.810
You don't use your breasts in track!

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:33.650
But if you want to read books,
you could join the literature club.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.320
I'm in it.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.330
What's this?

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:38.170
You trying to steal her from me, Sayoko?

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:39.820
I'm not trying to steal her.

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:40.980
Take this!

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:42.460
Take this! Take this!

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:44.170
You like it in the armpits?

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:48.720
Nozo-chan, stop it! Somebody save me!

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:48.720
<i>A club, huh?</i>

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:05.040
It's been a while.

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.660
It's been a while.

00:11:31.930 --> 00:11:34.570
I'd rather you didn't come to my school.

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:36.200
Can we talk?

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:39.200
I'm not getting in your car.

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:40.920
We can talk at a nearby café.

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:43.370
That's not very secure,

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.690
but if you insist.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:53.380
Was that her dad?

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:54.700
I don't know.

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:57.940
I'll get right to the point.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:02.300
A new small-scale unit is being set up under
JSDF Ground Component Command

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:06.110
to specialize in magical combat.

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:08.990
Its current name is M Squad.

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:10.280
I'll be running it.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:11.930
A squad?

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:13.170
It'll be very small,

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:15.530
but will given the same rank
as the other companies.

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:18.000
I'm not the only Magical Girl.

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:22.970
Kurumi's working at Ground Research and 
Development, at their integrated research lab.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:27.390
She's a magical warfare research
officer in Research Division #2.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:29.920
I see.

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.200
Everybody's doing their own thing, huh?

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.830
You're going to do it, too.

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:37.840
Come back, Asuka.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:39.840
I told you.

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:41.730
I'm not fighting anymore.

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:46.030
When I was in middle school,

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:47.630
I fought enough for one lifetime.

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:06.570
I'm home.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:19.440
Disas monsters?

00:13:31.230 --> 00:13:32.970
Where are my parents?

00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:35.500
Are they alive?

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.080
Of course, mu!

00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:42.810
Let's make a deal.

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:44.840
Give back my parents.

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:49.450
I'll do whatever I can.

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:51.860
We don't need to make a deal, mu.

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:55.520
We'll give you back your mom and dad, mu.

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:56.730
What?

00:13:57.080 --> 00:14:00.060
Little by little, mu.

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:07.320
<b>To Asuka-sama</b>

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.670
I'm not killing anybody
now that I'm in high school.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:30.670
When I do,

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:35.460
lots of people around me get killed, too.

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:39.980
I see.

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:47.380
How's your current school?

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:49.250
What's this about?

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:51.820
I'm your guardian, after all.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:55.540
That's just what the paperwork says.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.990
Well... It's not bad.

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:07.040
Asuka-san!

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:08.670
Hey, transfer student.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:09.930
Um...

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:11.520
Hata-san, Makino-san...

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:12.260
Hey,

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:15.630
who was that man you met with
in front of the school yesterday?

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:16.860
That's...

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:18.050
my dad.

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:20.320
I see. I'm so glad.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:22.310
For a moment, I thought
you were whoring yourself out.

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:23.310
Nozo-chan!

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:26.320
You're not supposed
to come out and say it!

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:33.450
Oh...

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:38.140
I was just thinking that
you two make a great pair.

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:40.170
We're childhood friends, after all.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:43.160
Well, now that we know
you're not a prostitute...

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:44.900
That's so rude!

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:46.640
Did you decide to join the track team?

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:48.730
No, not yet...

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:49.840
Nozo-chan!

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:54.470
Why not give it a try first?

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:05.570
Good work.

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:08.380
I like that look on your face.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:09.840
The look on my face?

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.910
You look like you worked off some stress.

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:15.880
It feels good to get a good workout, right?

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:18.990
Makino-san...

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.320
Just call me Nozomi.

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:23.510
Nozomi, have you been part of the
 track team for a long time?

00:16:23.990 --> 00:16:25.210
Since middle school.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.920
You know, you want to give your
all at the thing you're good at, right?

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:32.000
What you're good at, huh?

00:16:32.890 --> 00:16:34.580
Nozomi!

00:16:34.580 --> 00:16:35.600
Coming!

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:37.420
See you later.

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:41.810
Yeah.

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:43.000
That is a good look.

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:51.700
What is it?

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:54.280
I was just thinking that it's nice
to have something you like.

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:59.640
Actually, Asuka-san...

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:00.440
Oh,

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:03.960
what I do is just escapism.

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:08.920
I want to keep my mind occupied
as much as possible when I've got free time.

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:13.410
If I'm not constantly reading a book
and thinking about something,

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:15.180
it feels like I'll be crushed.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:18.400
Was I being weird again?

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:20.030
I think that's good.

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:26.700
"If you were a soldier,
and captured by the enemy,

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:29.040
escape would be your duty."

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:32.280
"When your heart and your
soul are trapped in a cage,

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:37.070
literature has the task, and the glory,
of providing you with an escape."

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:45.900
It's a line from this book!

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:47.770
Hey, Sayoko...

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:48.530
Yes?

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:52.830
Can I borrow that book?

00:17:54.160 --> 00:17:55.200
Okay!

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:58.740
<i>I don't know why,</i>

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:00.560
<i>but when I'm talking to these two,</i>

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:02.210
<i>I feel so at ease.</i>

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:05.720
<i>I quit being a Magical Girl.</i>

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:11.240
<i>All a person needs to do is
protect the people around them.</i>

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.150
<i>But...</i>

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:16.480
<i>Whenever I see something on the news,</i>

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:18.210
<i>I feel something in my heart.</i>

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:20.620
<i>If I'd tried harder,</i>

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:22.780
<i>could I have stopped it?</i>

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:26.880
<i>Am I just running away?</i>

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:28.940
<i>I always thought that, but...</i>

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:32.920
Sa—

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:42.540
Why did I hide?

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.630
Comrade Kim Kanth...

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:19.980
You almost killed me, too, you know.

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:22.600
I'm sorry. Security was tight.

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:24.850
We'll take you to the rendezvous point.

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:30.100
We're breaking through.

00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:39.780
We'll use the chaos
to cover our escape.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:42.860
Shoot some bystanders.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:56.320
<i>Kim Kanth, a terrorist with the 
East Asia United Front, fled during transport.</i>

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:59.080
<i>A special vehicle belonging to the
Metropolitan Riot Police was attacked.</i>

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:01.880
<i>Nearby PMs and PCs are to
head immediately to the scene,</i>

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:02.670
<i>and look out for weapons!</i>

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:07.260
What's going on?

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:14.220
<i>"I won't fight anymore."</i>

00:20:14.220 --> 00:20:16.140
<i>I thought I'd made my choice.</i>

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:19.880
<i>But no matter how
much I try to get away,</i>

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:22.200
<i>the battles come after me.</i>

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:25.780
<i>I heard the voice of destiny.</i>

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.200
<i>That's how it felt to me.</i>

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:37.960
<i>"Live your life for the
sake of those who died."</i>

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:40.820
<i>"Fight."</i>

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:50.770
Your luck ran out when you pointed a
gun at my friend somewhere I could see you.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:52.660
A M-Magical Girl?

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:54.060
What's one of them doing here?

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:15.660
I won't kill you.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:18.550
You'll go to the Public Safety Department's
 Foreign Affairs Section.

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:28.650
Oh.

00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:31.130
I guess she didn't retire.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:39.440
This is going to be fun, Abby.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:42.060
Yes, my queen.

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:46.880
<i>Once, Magical Girls</i>

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:51.000
<i>defeated the last boss, who led the 
enemies who tried to wipe out humanity.</i>

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:54.440
<i>But there are no endings in the real world.</i>

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:01.130
<i>Even after we defeated the last boss,</i>

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:03.930
<i>peace didn't return to the world.</i>

00:22:13.150 --> 00:22:16.940
<i>Our new battlefield is international crime,</i>

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:18.560
<i>indiscriminate terrorism,</i>

00:22:18.560 --> 00:22:19.600
<i>civil wars,</i>

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:20.870
<i>and other conflicts.</i>

00:22:21.700 --> 00:22:26.610
<i>A Magical Girl's battle never ends.</i>

00:23:57.910 --> 00:24:00.160
Asuka's returned to the battlefield, chu!

00:24:00.160 --> 00:24:01.790
And so has her old comrade,

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:04.910
the ditzy, easygoing nurse Magical Girl!

00:24:05.090 --> 00:24:05.590
Next time:

00:24:05.210 --> 00:24:08.000
<b>Daily Life and Comrades in Arms</b>

00:24:05.580 --> 00:24:07.070
"Daily Life and Comrades in Arms."

00:24:07.070 --> 00:24:11.450
With your Magical Karambit,
rip the bad guys to pieces, chu!
